{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115634",
      "title": "Interacting with Host Elements via @HostListener & @HostBinding",
      "lectureOrder": 117,
      "videoOrder": 111,
      "sourceHash": "3be9009260c64ca404a85e7daa831701b58314ab966f411f797667b05057fca2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 2.13,
          "en": "Now when it comes to working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 6.39,
          "en": "with that host element of an Angular component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.39,
          "end": 11.39,
          "en": "there are two other things you should know about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.4,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "And the first thing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "that when it comes to adding properties to the host element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "you can use this host setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "on the Component decorator object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 25.293,
          "en": "and that is the preferred way of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "But alternatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 31.89,
          "en": "you can also add a property to your component class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.89,
          "end": 35.16,
          "en": "and name it className, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.16,
          "end": 39.39,
          "en": "and set the value you wanna bind on your host element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.39,
          "end": 41.163,
          "en": "so control in my case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.48,
          "end": 47.403,
          "en": "And then decorate this with the HostBinding decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 52.053,
          "en": "which must be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.67,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "Now what HostBinding will do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 59.043,
          "en": "it will take a look at this property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 62.61,
          "en": "and it will then add it as a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 64.29,
          "en": "to the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.29,
          "end": 66.963,
          "en": "and set this as a value for that property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 71.4,
          "en": "Therefore, I can comment out host here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 73.173,
          "en": "and instead use HostBinding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.4,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "Now, I technically don't wanna use className here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 80.1,
          "en": "but class, and I could use it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.1,
          "end": 83.82,
          "en": "But to avoid any confusion with the built-in class keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.82,
          "end": 87.12,
          "en": "we might wanna use a slightly different property name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.12,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "And that's why HostBinding this decorator also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 94.56,
          "en": "takes an optional input, an optional argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "which allows you to define the actual property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 99.963,
          "en": "that should be bound as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.97999999999999,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "So now the value here will be set as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 108.03,
          "en": "for this class property with help of HostBinding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 110.643,
          "en": "even though the property name here is different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "You only need this argument here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.813,
          "en": "if you have a different property name, then you wanna bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 122.79,
          "en": "With that, if you reload, you got the same look as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.79,
          "end": 124.773,
          "en": "but now with HostBinding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 130.17,
          "en": "That being said, using HostBinding is discouraged though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.17,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "You should instead use the host property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 137.46,
          "en": "This feature just exists for backward compatibility reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "because in the past it was a common way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 144.72,
          "en": "of setting those host properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "Nowadays, you should prefer this host property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 150.483,
          "en": "on the Component decorator object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 156.99,
          "en": "There also is a HostListener decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.99,
          "end": 159.213,
          "en": "which you can import and use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.41,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "which allows you to bind a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 166.44299999999998,
          "en": "to an event to which you wanna listen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.34,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could add event binding here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "And for example, listen to a click event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 177.15,
          "en": "and then here define the method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.15,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "of the class that should be executed when that event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "So here, for example, we could add a onClick method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 187.317,
          "en": "and simply, console.log('Clicked').",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "And if you wanna trigger this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 195.09,
          "en": "whenever the host element is clicked, we can either do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.09,
          "end": 197.13,
          "en": "by adding this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.13,
          "end": 201.39,
          "en": "to our host object here in the Component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.39,
          "end": 204.24,
          "en": "So I'm using that event binding syntax here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.24,
          "end": 205.173,
          "en": "as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 207.96,
          "en": "And then also as a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.96,
          "end": 210.45,
          "en": "I define the code that should execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.45,
          "end": 213.153,
          "en": "when that click on the host element occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.05,
          "end": 215.57999999999998,
          "en": "So here I'm telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.57999999999998,
          "end": 219.09300000000002,
          "en": "that it should execute the onClick method of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 220.53,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 224.64,
          "en": "and you comment out HostListener for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 227.19,
          "en": "if you open your console here on the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 230.7,
          "en": "whenever I click into one of my controls,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 232.803,
          "en": "you see click gets logged here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "So you can also listen to events on the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 238.98,
          "en": "by using this syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.98,
          "end": 243.98,
          "en": "or as I mentioned, alternatively with HostListener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.99,
          "end": 246.24,
          "en": "Then you would directly assign the method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 246.24,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "that should be triggered as a value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 252.57,
          "en": "Though, you then also must pass an argument to HostListener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.57,
          "end": 255.213,
          "en": "and specify the event to which it should listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 256.8,
          "end": 258.69,
          "en": "So now you would be telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 262.23,
          "en": "that it should listen to click events on the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.23,
          "end": 265.773,
          "en": "and trigger that method whenever such a click occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 272.49,
          "en": "With that, if I save this and reload, we also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.49,
          "end": 275.13,
          "en": "that clicked output in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 275.13,
          "end": 277.473,
          "en": "as I click on those controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.56,
          "end": 285.39,
          "en": "So that again, is an alternative to using this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 285.39,
          "end": 289.47,
          "en": "Now, I personally actually prefer this alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.47,
          "end": 292.92,
          "en": "I think it looks a bit cleaner than defining this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.92,
          "end": 295.92,
          "en": "but the Angular team recommends this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.92,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "which is why I'm showing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 300.51,
          "en": "and recommending it to you here in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.51,
          "end": 301.65,
          "en": "So that's how you could listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 301.65,
          "end": 305.04,
          "en": "to events on your host elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.04,
          "end": 307.65,
          "en": "Of course, we now also have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.65,
          "end": 310.5,
          "en": "that this onClick method exists though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.5,
          "end": 312.363,
          "en": "otherwise this will fail.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
